scenes is right now we're in hiatus time  for network TV shows I think this would  be a good point for me to sort of touch  base and give sort of a half way rating  of some of the stuff I've been watching  now none of this stuff I've had a  passionate enough feeling about to do  episode by episode reviews like I have  would say doctor who but you know what I  think is worth touching on since we're  kind of in the low between their first  and second halves the first one I want  to talk about is one I did not think I  was ever going to want to talk about  again Gotham if you saw my original tag  team review that i did with Ryan Daley  was not a fan of that pilot still not a  fan of that pilot however I have turned  around on the show even the second  episode things were already looking  better by the third episode which was  balloon man that was the one that turned  me around and I now actually look  forward to that show and I'm looking  forward to when it comes back below man  really was the one that turned me around  because it started to accomplish a  number of things it got a dynamic  working between Gordon and Bullock that  was more dynamic and more interesting as  they were starting to come to terms with  each other because initially they were  just banging head so hard that it was  annoying Gordon was starting to operate  in the world a little bit better he's  started to become slightly more  compromised by the situation I mean he's  still the white knight relatively  speaking but the shines off him a little  bit he's becoming more attuned to the  reality of where he is and not having  him so naively and steadfastly blindly  just going doing the right thing it  makes him more dynamic and makes it more  interesting and the beloved man also  marked the point at which they started  to bring in some of them more fun and  somewhat ridiculous elements that you  get out of a comic book world I mean a  guy a vigilante who kills people by  attaching them to weather balloons  that's kind of nuts and in that fun  comic book way and it really wasn't  until that episode that the show started  to embrace that side of it gone pretty  grim pretty gritty pretty cop show  initially and I know that's the pitch of  the show but it seemed like why would  this even have to be set in Gotham if  you're not going to embrace any aspect  of that world well they started to of  that episode and they've taken some good  aspects of that going forward the  penguin continues to be the absolute  the show but as I said Jim Gordon has  actually grown on me there been some  other good ones I really like the  interpretation of Victor Zsasz that we  got although I really could have done  without the completely superfluous  henchmen they paired him with I like a  lot of the behind-the-scenes power plays  that are going on between the mobsters I  like that it's not a flat-out war  because we've seen that a lot in movies  TV what have you an all-out mob war but  to see these two crime families of  moroni and Falcone existing in the same  world and obviously continually trying  to undermine and undercut and take over  ground from the other but not being able  to do so out in the open and still sort  of having this grudging sort of  understanding it's not really a truce  and they'd like to knock each other out  but they can't thing is interesting and  much more dynamic than I think we tend  to get Alfred's working much better as a  character he was a little schizophrenic  at first cuz they were really  reconciling his paternal instincts with  his much tougher sort of ex-military  vibe that they had decided to saddle  them with which there's nothing wrong  with that choice but they weren't really  marrying those aspects and they found  that rhythm with him since then and the  show as a whole has found its approach  to procedurals that it's now working  pretty well while still having the  continuing sort of story of largely the  crime families battling it out for  control so like I said that I really  turned around on the show and I do enjoy  it at this point there are a couple of  things that are still not working though  the big one is Barbara she has become  exactly what I was afraid she was gonna  be which is the hangar on baggage  girlfriend that heroes tend to get  saddled with she's not an asset to him  she's a liability and that is made it's  so explicit by it by an episode where he  sends her away because he's about to do  something that is gonna put him and  direct extreme danger he doesn't want  her anywhere near it what does she do  she comes back and it wasn't like one of  those cases like go see your mother I  can't tell you why she knew what he was  gonna do she knew he was in danger she  knew that her being around was gonna  make it harder for him and she came back  at that point she just became completely  worthless as a character in my eyes and  she hasn't gotten any better since the  handling of Bruce Wayne has also been a  little bit off it's been better  than I thought it was going to be partly  because they're putting on ice emphasis  on the detective side of Batman because  when batman begins in the nola movies we  got a very heavy emphasis on the combat  side of batman basically sort of the  ninja aspect of Batman and his role as a  detective was fairly underplayed now you  can't have this young version of Bruce  Wayne just kicking the butts of  criminals but you can't have him develop  his mind in his deductive skills and  they've had him doing that and it's  worked very well things get a little bit  off for me when they start having him  interact especially with other kids  because they've made him I think that  just trying to go for socially awkward  he comes off honestly as some degree of  autistic just with the extent that he  takes things literally doesn't seem to  understand normal human emotional  interactions he has to get Alfred  explaining stuff to him it just seems  off they made him a little too removed  from a normal child's life I think then  was warranted Selina Kyle cat cheese I  also kind of back and forth for me she  works fairly well when she's interacting  with adults when she's working with  Bruce and not so much i think partments  just add the line reading she gives  their their clunky part of that might be  the writing but when they try and have  her be a kid it doesn't work so well  then when they've got her sort of  functioning as a story element you know  being a character with information and  characters breaking into thing she works  better although I really really cringed  when they brought back ivy because this  was a throw-in and an odd that just it  did seems to serve no purpose and it  looks like they probably are going to  bring her back to some extent and I  don't understand why Edward nygma though  surprisingly has worked pretty well for  me the few times that they've put a more  emphasis and lingered on a bit more I  he's a little braiding but terms of his  function in the world I think it was a  pretty interesting call making him a  forensics guy that everybody's kind of  annoyed by I am now a fan of the show  but the mid-season finale really had a  lot of the problems that I  had back in the pile of that the show  had actually sort of gotten over but  then they all came back things like what  I've talked about Barbara Bruce not  really working so well bring back ivy  these nods to things in the comic but  not actually integrating them in any way  that felt meaningful so that sort of  showed me that the show can still dip  back into those early habits now even  that I'm so did not do it as badly as  the pilot the pilot was just a mess but  I'm gonna give props to the show it has  grown and has grown on me and I feel  it's actually pretty strong at this  point you know it's pretty rare for me  to see a show that just does not work in  front end and then gets steadily better  after that especially within the same  season I've seen some shows the first  seeds is not great then it gets better  the second season this was one within  that first season it even turn around  have you ever had an experience like  that what was a show that for you  started out week got better did it do it  within the first season did it take a  little while whatever it was drop  something down in the comments and let's  talk about it until next time this  council is adjourned

